{
  "comment": "The boxes and the links that the command line draws, and that the editor must draw, for saved views of viewpoint `map` and layer `application` that carry `links` (wave 026, run 0199, DEC-8 and DEC-9 of the TDD, REQ-3). One file, read by map-links-shared.test.js (the page Applications, the page of a view and the story scene of a step, over the embedded kernel and a fake layout engine) and by MapLinksSharedTest.java (`views generate -i` on a temporary copy). The file was written from the command line, the reference: the packaged jar of this run ran `views generate -w <copy>/.archicode.yaml --plateau <plateau> [--against <against>] -i <view>` on a temporary copy of `workspace` to which the view of each case was added as a manifest in `folder` (no shipped file carries `links`, DEC-9), and the boxes and links are those read from the written file (`views-<plateau>`, `views-<plateau>-vs-<against>` or `views-<plateau>-<facet>`). A box is the id of its item, a link is `from -> to` between two boxes (a pair drawn twice is listed once); both lists are sorted. A case has `plateau`, `against` (the comparison, absent for none), `facet` (a facet of the settings, absent for none), `properties` (the properties of the view, written as given) and `drawn`: false means the command line draws nothing (it skips the view with the warning in `cli`). `cli` is what the command line said on its error output. The editor says in these cases that nothing is drawn (the page Applications: 'Nothing is drawn: none of the relationships ticked is in this plateau.'; the page of a view: 'None of the relationships it shows is in the plateau “p”.').",
